{"name":"Gecko","hex":"#9d913c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gecko","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Gekkonidae – synonym of Gekko (true geckos)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gecko"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gecko","blocks":[{"text":"Geckos are small, mostly carnivorous lizards that have a wide distribution, found on every continent except Antarctica. Belonging to the suborder Gekkota, geckos are found in warm climates. They range from 1.6 to 67 centimetres in length. They are the most species-rich group of lizards, with nearly 2,000 different species of geckos existing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Phelsuma_l._laticauda.jpg/330px-Phelsuma_l._laticauda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko","wikidata":"Q16546828"},{"title":"Gecko (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Gecko is a browser engine developed by Mozilla. It is used in the Firefox browser, the Thunderbird email client, and in a discontinued state on AOL's Netscape 6, Netscape 7, Netscape Browser and Netscape Navigator 9; this is alongside many other projects."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(software)","wikidata":"Q487834"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Gecko_foot_on_glass.JPG/500px-Gecko_foot_on_glass.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Gecko_foot_on_glass.JPG/1280px-Gecko_foot_on_glass.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Gecko_foot_on_glass.JPG/500px-Gecko_foot_on_glass.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close-up of the underside of a gecko's foot as it walks on vertical glass","link":"